kgfax.exe
kgfax.exe.c
kgfax.exe.asm
readme.txt
extracted/
.DS_Store

# Personal working notes — not for publication (medical info, private
# analysis references). See docs/README.md "What gets published vs. stays
# private".
SESSION-LOG.md
AGENTS.md
START-HERE.md

# Icon design references (work-in-progress, not source)
Gemini_Generated_Image_*.png

# Local machine state (device index, window position), next to the exe
# like the original. kgfax.ini is the original program's file, kept as a
# reference and read once for migration; isobar.ini is ours.
kgfax.ini
isobar.ini

# CMake build directory (created by cmake -B build)
build/
build-*/

# Decoded test output and scratch files (regenerable from the sample WAV)
out.pgm
out.png
out.syn

# Full 9.6-minute test recording (97 MB — too big for git). The 30-second
# excerpt jmh-sample-short.wav is committed instead and is what CI runs
# against. Keep the full file locally for deeper testing.
jmh sample.wav

# Full 15-minute 12 kHz off-air JMH recording (22 MB), supplied 2026-08-01.
# GitHub would take it, but git history is permanent and every clone and CI
# checkout pays for it — so, as with "jmh sample.wav", the 60-second excerpt
# jmh-offair-12k.wav is committed instead and is what CI runs against.
# It is the sample the sync-detector findings in DEVIATIONS.md #16 were
# measured against; keep the full file locally for deeper testing. A second
# 60-second excerpt, jmh-slew-12k.wav (50..110 s), is committed too — that
# stretch runs on the fallback and guards the sync-strip split (slew-test).
HDSDR_20260801_032125Z_13987kHz_AF.wav

# Full 18.8-minute 16 kHz recording of two back-to-back JMH HIMAWARI IR
# charts (36 MB), supplied 2026-08-02. Same reasoning as above: the
# 90-second excerpt jmh-phasing-16k.wav is committed instead and is what CI
# runs against. It is the recording that exposed the phase-runaway bug the
# excerpt now guards (cli/phasing-test.cpp); keep the full file locally.
FAXSignal.wav

# KiwiSDR recordings of a JMH HIMAWARI IR chart and a test chart, taken
# 2026-08-03 (the .m4a originals, ~42 MB, and their .wav conversions,
# ~134 MB). Same reasoning as above: the 60-second excerpt
# jmh-himawari-12k.wav (300..360 s of the himawari reception, resampled to
# 12 kHz) is committed instead and is what CI runs against. That excerpt is
# the only fixture whose video is a PHOTO rather than a chart, which is what
# cli/satellite-test.cpp exists to guard; keep the full files locally.
himawari.m4a
test chart.m4a
jmh-kiwi-himawari.wav
jmh-kiwi-testchart.wav

# Decoded output from those recordings (regenerable; see satellite-test).
kiwi-*.pgm
himawari-*.png

# Stray source video (an internet recording used for early hand-tests;
# unreferenced by any code or doc).
videoplayback.mp4

# Editor/agent scratch
.zcode/
.kimi-code/
.claude/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Office lock/temp files. Matters here because opening the copyrighted
# readme.txt in Word drops a ~$readme.txt beside it, which the readme.txt
# rule above does NOT cover.
~$*

# Chat/session export dumps (private working material)
*-export-session*.md
session-*.md

